# Architecture — custom store, golden path

## Context

`app/` uses a hand-written store, not a library. `app/src/store.ts` exposes
`createStore()` returning `{ getState, dispatch, subscribe }` and is the ONLY
sanctioned way state changes. `app/src/types.ts` holds `AppState`, `Task`, and
the `Action` discriminated union; `app/src/reducer.ts` is the pure reducer.
See `materials/architecture-brief.md` for the source of truth.

## Rule

- Change state ONLY via `store.dispatch(action)`; never assign to `state` or
  task fields directly.
- Extend behavior along the golden path: add an `Action` variant in
  `app/src/types.ts` → handle it in `app/src/reducer.ts` → add an action creator
  in `app/src/actions.ts` → add a colocated `*.test.ts`.
- Read state through selectors in `app/src/selectors.ts`, not `state.tasks`
  directly, when adding derived reads.
- NEVER introduce Redux, Zustand, MobX, Jotai, Recoil, or any state library.
- NEVER replace the custom store with `useState`/hooks or a global mutable object.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rEi "redux|zustand|mobx|jotai|recoil" app/` returns zero matches.
2. New action `type` strings exist in `app/src/types.ts` `Action` union AND have
   a matching `case` in `app/src/reducer.ts`.
3. Every new action has a creator in `app/src/actions.ts` and a colocated test.
4. `cd app && npm test` is green.

